The following activities have been conducted under the UNODC-WCO Global Container Control Programme in Kazakhstan under SOU 2.1.2.2: 
-	Official opening of Air Cargo Control Unit at “Zhetysu” Customs post in Almaty international airport; 
-	Visit of CCP team of UNODC in Afghanistan to the Port Control Unit at “Altynkol zhol” Customs post (Khorgos area) with the aim of national consultations on inter-regional cooperation between Kazakh and Afghan Customs; 
-	Advanced Online Training on Evidence handling and Intelligence for the Customs officers of the Port Control Units at “Morport” and “Altynkol zhol” Customs posts and Air Cargo Control Unit at “Zhetysu” Customs post. 
-	Mentorship programme for Customs officers of ACCU at Almaty airport, 4-9 October 2021, Almaty; 
-	Training for Kazakh Customs on the use of portable drug analyzer TruNarc Raman in Vienna, 16-18 November 2021. 
-	A series of national and regional trainings on course on modern control techniques in holding search operations on vehicles, trains and goods crossing the state border were held in Almaty, in April and October 2021.

The project aims to demonstrate that straw combustion is a viable solution for carbon neutral heating and electricity production, and to generate political will to use this abundant renewable resource in the energy system. The project will help to create framework for building a new sustainable biomass industry based on straw in Kazakhstan. This framework will envisage expanding from a pilot region to the whole country scaling up the clean energy production capacity from briquettes for households to medium and large-scale technologies and quality. The project will also emphasize the social impact of these intervention by studying the needs and attracting at least 50% SMEs led by women or where 50% employees are women interested in straw briquette production.
The project will:
a) Assess the current and potential market and investment needs of SMEs interested in straw briquette production (sustainability study);
b) Develop and pilot the system to support investments in "straw to energy" projects with focus on women-led SMEs
c) Develop a framework for the subsequent transformation of the pilot intervention into a sustainable national biomass fuel production industry;
d) Organize gender equality and environmental education courses in partnership with local government and CSOs for project beneficiaries and companies.

Q1-Q2 2022: - A national consultant to support the upcoming Public Hearings in October 2022 was identified based on the developed Concept Note and agreed by all national governmental and non-governmental and international counterparts. 
- Expert support and technical assistance to the OST sites visits provided and are being implemented in partnership with the Republican Mental Health Centre, Country Coordination Committee on Work with International Organizations on HIV and TB issues (CCM) and national non-governmental counterparts. As a result of the OST sites visits to Pavlodar, Ekibastuz and Uralsk organized in partnership with the Republican Mental Health Centre, the Amansaulyk Public Foundation, the Kazakhstan Union of People Living with HIV, relevant information on the problems and issues the OST programme patients have been collected based on focus group discussion with the patients and medical personnel. The OST sites visits to Almaty, Karaganda and Temirtau have been postponed until August due to the delays in procurement of methadone. 
-       National consultant to support the Public Hearings in October 2022 is being engaged;
-	Monitoring visits to the OST sites in Almaty, Pavlodar, Ekibastuz, Karaganda, Temirtau and Uralsk have been completed; 
-	The outcomes of the survey of the OST programme patients are being analyzed.

